      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Alice Lucas’s rhymed paraliturgical translation of Hashkivenu, was first published in her <tei:hi rend="italic">The Jewish Year</tei:hi> (1898), page 74, under the title “At Evening.” Her variation of Hashkivenu seems to me to be a combination of the Sefaradi version (beginning with ‘Hashkivenu Avinu’) and the Ashkenazi version (with the two ‘ki El’ near the end), but I am not familiar with all the variations she may have had before her. The final blessing is omitted in her translation.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_36180_notes"/>
